      {
        "id": "ed-note-sync", "kind": "note",
        "text": "Everything on the left is a caller waiting for an answer. Everything on the right runs after that answer was already sent.",
        "x": 16, "y": 248, "width": 236, "size": "md", "font": "hand"
      },
      {
        "id": "ed-note-fanout", "kind": "note",
        "text": "One event becomes five pieces of work here, each read by its own consumer. Turn the load up and watch the audit log: it takes 40ms a message and falls behind while the four beside it keep up, and nobody calling the API sees a thing.",
        "x": 1160, "y": 16, "width": 300, "size": "md", "font": "hand"
      },
      {
        "id": "ed-note-cold", "kind": "note",
        "text": "The report function starts cold. The first call after a quiet spell pays 350ms of startup, then stays warm for ten seconds. Watch the first burst after the timer fires.",
